<!--
  The Kaaba, as a mark on the Qibla dial: the silhouette. Its hizam (the band) and its door
  are a separate drawable, ic_kaaba_detail.xml, drawn on top of this one in gold.

  Shared between the phone and the watch, because they draw the same dial twice and a
  shape that drifts between them is exactly the kind of gap this project has been bitten
  by before.

  Two drawables rather than one path with the band and door cut out of it by the even-odd
  rule. The cut-out version was written first and looked correct in review, and it was
  wrong: a hole shows whatever is behind the mark, and what is behind the mark is the
  needle. The Qibla needle ends inside the cube, so it appeared as a green streak through
  the doorway and across the band, which read as a rendering fault rather than a building.
  Opaque silhouette plus opaque detail cannot do that, whatever it is drawn over.

  Deliberately a flat elevation and not a photograph or a perspective render. A photograph
  would be someone else's copyright, would weigh more than the rest of the app's drawables
  put together, and would be unreadable at the ~19dp this is drawn at on a 1.2" watch. The
  silhouette, the band and the raised door are the three things that make it recognisable;
  everything else is detail that disappears at that size anyway.

  **Geometry, redrawn 15 Aug 2026 from the building's own measurements** rather than from
  round numbers, after the owner reported the mark looking wrong. In the 24x24 viewport the
  wall is x 5..19 and y 3.5..20 — 14 wide by 16.5 tall, a ratio of 0.85 against the real
  front face's 11.03m by 13.1m, which is 0.84. It stands on the wider marble plinth, the
  shadharwan, which oversails it by 1.5 units either side.

  The previous version was 15 by 17 starting at y 3, with the band at y 7.5. Nothing about
  it was far wrong on paper and it read, at size, as a **shopfront**: the band sat high
  enough to leave a thin strip of cube above it, and because the band was painted in the
  page colour rather than gold, that strip separated visually and became an awning over a
  shop sign. Lowering the band and colouring it fixed the same complaint twice over. See
  ic_kaaba_detail.xml, and HANDOVER §10 for the screenshots.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FF000000"
        android:pathData="M5,3.5h14v16.5h-14z M3.5,20h17v1.4h-17z" />
</vector>
